abstract: >-
  An educational MRI simulator distributed as a single HTML file that runs
  offline in a web browser. Changing the acquisition parameters of 60
  sequences on 12 analytic virtual phantoms updates the simulated image, scan
  time, SNR, SAR, tissue-contrast curves and k-space filling in real time;
  tissue signals can optionally be computed with extended phase graphs (EPG)
  or a Bloch-equivalent per-pixel mode. It also maps sequence and option names
  across six scanner vendors with confidence flags, offers a learning mode, and
  is available in Japanese, English and Simplified Chinese. It is an
  educational approximation, not a medical device, and is not intended for
  clinical use.
